From: Legodev <legodevgit@mailbox.org>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: fsl: bman: publish RCR tail before the valid bit

An RCR entry spans two cache lines on e500. Flush its second half before
publishing the verb in the first half, so BMan cannot consume stale buffer
addresses while the second line is still dirty in the CPU cache.

Signed-off-by: Legodev <legodevgit@mailbox.org>

diff --git a/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/bman.c b/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/bman.c
--- a/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/bman.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/bman.c
@@ -367,8 +367,12 @@
 	DPAA_ASSERT(rcr->busy);
 	DPAA_ASSERT(rcr->pmode == bm_rcr_pvb);
 	DPAA_ASSERT(rcr->available >= 1);
-	dma_wmb();
 	rcursor = rcr->cursor;
+#if defined(CONFIG_PPC) && L1_CACHE_BYTES == 32
+	flush_dcache_range((unsigned long)rcursor + 32,
+			   (unsigned long)rcursor + 64);
+#endif
+	dma_wmb();
 	rcursor->_ncw_verb = myverb | rcr->vbit;
 	dpaa_flush(rcursor);
 	rcr_inc(rcr);
